<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-2841] shell interpreter complained that working directory &apos;.&apos; can not be found in docker enviroment</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-2841</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;I installed zeppelin v7.0 on a centos6.5 based image, which made an new image.&lt;br/&gt;
I started the new image with CMD  &lt;ins&gt;_${ZEPPELIN_HOME}/bin/zeppelin.sh --config ${ZEPPELIN_CONF_DIR} _&lt;/ins&gt; . It stared and work normally until I run an shell script.&lt;br/&gt;
An script as simple as &apos;ls&apos;. It failed and the log said that working directory &apos;.&apos; can not be&lt;br/&gt;
found.&lt;br/&gt;
I add a line of code to set current working directory to USER`s home, and it works.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
